{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q3gZ4Rh58iTpQJLvGxG8D6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Pulitzer Prize winners 1950 fiction novel authors\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"www.britannica.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/print/article/2227349\"},{\"title\":\"pulitzer prize winners fiction\",\"url\":\"https://www.teachervision.com/pulitzer-prize-winners-fiction\"},{\"title\":\"b guthrie\",\"url\":\"https://www.pulitzer.org/winners/b-guthrie\"},{\"title\":\"ernest hemingway\",\"url\":\"https://www.pulitzer.org/winners/ernest-hemingway\"},{\"title\":\"Pulitzer Prize for Fiction: A Pinnacle of American Literature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nocloo.com/pulitzer-prize-for-fiction-winners-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Thursday, November 14\",\"url\":\"https://awardsarchive.com/category/all-book-awards/book-awards/pulitzer-prize/pulitzer-prize-fiction/page/4\"},{\"title\":\"Pulitzer Prize for Fiction\",\"url\":\"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Pulitzer_Prize_for_Fiction\"},{\"title\":\"1950 Pulitzer Prize\",\"url\":\"https://ipfs.aleph.im/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/1950_Pulitzer_Prize.html\"},{\"title\":\"Pulitzer Prize for Fiction\",\"url\":\"https://www.fantasticfiction.com/awards/pulitzer-prize/pulitzer-prize-for-fiction/1950.htm\"},{\"title\":\"THE PULITZER PRIZE FOR FICTION\",\"url\":\"https://www.rosecityreader.com/2019/10/list-pulitzer-prize-for-fiction.html?m=1\"},{\"title\":\"Pulitzer Prize Winners\",\"url\":\"https://dpi.state.wi.us/talkingbooks/services/reading-lists/pulitzer-winners\"},{\"title\":\"1950-1959 Winners\",\"url\":\"https://app.studyraid.com/en/read/110423/5028613/1950-1959-winners\"},{\"title\":\"Monday, May 12\",\"url\":\"https://www.awardsarchive.com/category/all-book-awards/book-awards/pulitzer-prize/page/13\"},{\"title\":\"1950 pulitzer prize\",\"url\":\"https://www.doc.surf/wiki/1950-pulitzer-prize\"},{\"title\":\"Jump to content\",\"url\":\"https://wiki.riteme.site/wiki/Pulitzer_Prize_for_Novel\"},{\"title\":\"Anexo:Premios Pulitzer de 1950\",\"url\":\"https://es.wikipedia.com/wiki/1950_Pulitzer_Prize\"},{\"title\":\"1950 Pulitzer Prize\",\"url\":\"https://wiki.riteme.site/wiki/1950_Pulitzer_Prize\"}]\n\nThe 1950 Pulitzer Prize for Fiction went to A. B. Guthrie Jr. for *The Way West*. Several sources agree on this, and it's the only 1950 fiction winner the results name.\n\n- Guthrie's novel was published in 1949 by William Sloane Associates, and the prize is listed for the 1950 award year. A. B. Guthrie (1901–1991) The Way West William Sloane Associates (1949) Western fiction Indiana\n- The book is a sequel to *The Big Sky* and follows a frontiersman's return to the West in 1846. The sequel to THE BIG SKY, this celebrated novel charts a frontiersman's return to the untamed West in 1846.\n- The award year and publication year differ because the prize honors books from the previous calendar year. Because the award is for books published in the preceding calendar year, the \"Year\" column links to the preceding year in literature.\n\nFor context, the 1951 winner was Conrad Richter's *The Town*. Conrad Richter | The Town | Alfred A. Knopf (1950) | Novel | Pennsylvania\n\nThe results contained some inconsistent table entries from mirror sites, so the Guthrie attribution is best checked against the official Pulitzer.org winners page, which the search did not return for fiction.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"005dff10-28d1-43ff-bcba-2ab995b1a422","uuid":"e956af2f-a37b-4e67-bca5-2370823453fc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:35:48.759Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Pulitzer Prize winners 1950 fiction novel authors","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XDRe6sPMfU3PwraK3Fd7oj","content":[{"title":"www.britannica.com","url":"https://www.britannica.com/print/article/2227349"},{"title":